Motorola MC68040 Floating-Point Software Package
==============================================

These 42 files are unmodified copies from Linux v6.12, commit
adc218676eef25575469234709c2d87185ca223a, arch/m68k/fpsp040:
https://github.com/torvalds/linux/tree/adc218676eef25575469234709c2d87185ca223a/arch/m68k/fpsp040

Every imported file was checked against its upstream Git blob hash.
Motorola's complete copyright and permission notice is retained in README.
The Linux Makefile and Linux-specific skeleton.S are not included.

Executor's adapter/installer live in ../../src/runtime, with the image builder
under ../../tools and integration tests under ../../tests, outside this directory.
They assemble and relocate the original guest code; they do
not replace the package's arithmetic with host floating-point functions.
Generated objects, linked images and C includes belong in
../../obj/src/runtime/generated; test outputs belong in ../../obj/tests/fpsp.

Run bash syn68k/tests/check-core.sh fpsp from the workspace root. This needs
m68k-linux-gnu GCC/binutils in addition to the normal Windows build tools.
Executor installs the package in system memory after its final vector reset.
Real exceptions are forwarded to the previous vector handlers. Motorola's notice
is staged beside Executor under licenses/motorola-fpsp.txt.
Passing the tests does not establish complete FPSP exception compatibility.
